{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/DirectedIncidenceGraphView"},"abstract":[{"text":"A directed hypergraph’s incidence graph, read lazily from its storage: a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"text":" on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< n + m"},{"text":" whose vertex ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i < n"},{"text":" is the hypergraph’s vertex","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"index ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i"},{"text":" and whose vertex ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"n + p"},{"text":" is hyperedge ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"text":", with an arc ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i → n + p"},{"text":" for each source","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i"},{"text":" of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"n + p → j"},{"text":" for each target ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"j"},{"text":". A vertex on both sides of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"text":" gives the 2-cycle","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i → n + p → i"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedIncidenceGraphView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedHypergraph","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedHypergraph","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols18DirectedHypergraphP"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Edges."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" Positions "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< P_s"},{"type":"text","text":" are the source incidences, hyperedge by hyperedge in index"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order and within one in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sourceIndices"},{"type":"text","text":" order, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"P_s + q"},{"type":"text","text":" is target incidence "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"q"},{"type":"text","text":", in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same order. A per-incidence array is indexed by edge position. A view is a snapshot, so its own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"positions never change, but they are valid for the hypergraph only until its next mutation:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the view of the mutated hypergraph numbers the incidences afresh (on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inserting one cell shifts every later incidence by one)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The LabeledGraph law.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" Every index member reads the base’s rows, shifted where they hold"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hyperedges: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successorIndices(ofIndex: i)"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outHyperedgeIndices(ofIndex: i)"},{"type":"text","text":" plus n, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"n + p"},{"type":"text","text":" it is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"targetIndices(ofHyperedgeAt: p)"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"predecessorIndices"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inHyperedgeIndices"},{"type":"text","text":" plus n, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sourceIndices"},{"type":"text","text":". So graph algorithms run on the view without"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hashing a vertex. The view does not offer "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_withSuccessorIndexRows"},{"type":"text","text":", whose contract needs edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"positions in row order."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Costs.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" As for ","type":"text"},{"code":"IncidenceGraphView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": O(1) reads on ","type":"text"},{"code":"IncidenceList","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which stores its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"incidences; on another base a hyperedge’s incidence numbers are a range, O(1), ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges[q]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"binary-searches and selects by rank, O(log m + ⌈n\/64⌉) on ","type":"text"},{"code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and a vertex’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"outEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"inEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is computed from ","type":"text"},{"code":"_memberRank","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", O(d·⌈n\/64⌉) on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/s8Se